      place: "Riksdag (Riksdagshuset), Helgeandsholmen, Stockholm, Sweden",
      body: "Sweden's Datalag (SFS 1973:289) was issued on 11 May 1973 after the Riksdag adopted the government's bill that spring. It barred anyone from setting up or keeping a computerised personal register without the permission of a new authority, Datainspektionen (the Data Inspection Board), which was established from 1 July 1973; the permit provisions took effect a year later, after a constitutional amendment. The Liberal member of parliament Kerstin Anér was a leading advocate.",
