          url: "https://aspe.hhs.gov/reports/records-computers-rights-citizens",
          quote: "Although there is nothing inherently unfair in trading some measure of privacy for a benefit, both parties to the exchange should participate in setting the terms.",
          note: "Summary and Recommendations section. The same page states: 'the report recommends the enactment of a Federal \"Code of Fair Information Practice\" for all automated personal data systems. The Code rests on five basic principles...' and that it 'opposes the establishment of such an identification scheme at this time.'",
