      place: "United States Capitol, Washington, D.C.",
      body: "The Privacy Act of 1974 (Public Law 93-579, 88 Stat. 1896) was approved on 31 December 1974 and took effect on 27 September 1975 as the principal law governing how US federal agencies handle personal information. Congress passed it in the final week of the 93rd Congress, in the wake of Watergate and COINTELPRO, relying on the HEW report's code of fair information practices. President Gerald Ford's signing statement, released at Vail, Colorado, called it 'an historic beginning'; the act also created an advisory Privacy Protection Study Commission.",
