      place: "Le Monde newsroom, rue des Italiens, Paris, France",
      body: "On 21 March 1974 Le Monde published Philippe Boucher's article '\"Safari\" ou la chasse aux Français', describing an Iris-80 computer being brought into service for the Interior Ministry and the SAFARI operation for the individual identification of all 52 million French people. Citing a very senior magistrate, the article reported that police services held some 100 million index cards in 400 files. By a decree of 8 November 1974 the President charged a commission attached to the Minister of Justice with proposing, within six months, measures to ensure that computerisation respected private life and individual and public liberties; its report was signed in Paris on 27 June 1975.",
