      place: "Parlament, Vienna, Austria",
      body: "Austria's Datenschutzgesetz (DSG), federal law of 18 October 1978, was published in the Bundesgesetzblatt on 28 November 1978 as BGBl. Nr. 565/1978. Its first article, a constitutional provision headed 'Grundrecht auf Datenschutz' (fundamental right to data protection), gave everyone a claim to the confidentiality of personal data concerning them where they have an interest worthy of protection, plus rights of access to automatically processed data. Most of the act came into force on 1 January 1980.",
