          url: "https://www.w3.org/TR/2002/REC-P3P-20020416/",
          quote: "The Platform for Privacy Preferences Project (P3P) enables Web sites to express their privacy practices in a standard format that can be retrieved automatically and interpreted easily by user agents.",
          note: "Section 1, Introduction, continues: 'Thus users need not read the privacy policies at every site they visit. Although P3P provides a technical mechanism for ensuring that users can be informed about privacy policies before they release personal information, it does not provide a technical mechanism for making sure sites act according to their policies.'",
