      body: "In Justice K.S. Puttaswamy (Retd) v. Union of India, decided on 24 August 2017, a nine-judge bench held that the right to privacy is protected as an intrinsic part of the right to life and personal liberty under Article 21 and the freedoms of Part III of the Constitution. The reference arose from a constitutional challenge to Aadhaar, the national biometric identity database; the court noted that the government had set up a committee under Justice B.N. Srikrishna to review data-protection norms.",
