      body: "From 25 May 2018 the GDPR applied across the EU. Consent had to be as easy to withdraw as to give (Article 7(3)), and the most serious infringements became punishable by fines of up to €20 million or 4% of worldwide annual turnover, whichever is higher (Article 83(5)). On the first day, the privacy group noyb filed four complaints against Google (Android), Facebook, WhatsApp and Instagram over 'forced consent', as 'consent boxes' popped up across the web.",
      lat: 50.8435,
      lng: 4.3826,
