      place: "IETF Administration LLC, Wilmington, Delaware",
      body: "The IETF approved the charter of the AI Preferences working group to standardise a vocabulary for expressing how content may be used for AI training and use, and ways to attach those preferences through robots.txt and HTTP headers. It followed earlier publisher-side efforts such as the W3C community group's TDM Reservation Protocol (final report 10 May 2024). The charter puts technical enforcement and auditing out of scope; the vocabulary draft (version 08, 14 September 2026) says a recipient 'has a choice whether to follow those preferences' and that contracts may override them.",
