      headline: "A physician swears to keep what he sees",
      narrative: "The Greek Oath attributed to Hippocrates ends its list of duties with a promise that whatever the physician sees or hears in the lives of patients, in practice or not, and which ought not to be spoken of outside, will be kept secret as private. Its date and authorship are uncertain: it has long been placed at the end of the fifth or start of the fourth century BCE, but some scholars argue for a Hellenistic origin.",
