      phase: "walls",
      headline: "Ask before you enter; do not spy",
      narrative: "Two Medinan passages of the Qur'an set household privacy rules: 24:27 tells believers not to enter houses other than their own until they have sought welcome and greeted the occupants, and 49:12 says 'do not spy' on one another. A hadith collected by al-Bukhari ties the permission rule to the eye: a man who peeped through a hole into the Prophet's dwelling was told that asking permission to enter was enjoined because of that sight.",
