      date: "27 November 1765",
      phase: "castle",
      headline: "Papers are a man's dearest property",
      narrative: "King's messengers acting on a warrant from the Earl of Halifax entered John Entick's house on 11 November 1762 and carried off his papers. Delivering judgment for Entick on Wednesday 27 November 1765, Lord Camden (Charles Pratt) held there was no law to justify the search. A newly published contemporaneous report by Edward Moore has Camden saying private papers are 'the only way of concealing a man's most valuable Secrets' and are 'his dearest property'.",
