      narrative: "The First Congress proposed twelve amendments on 25 September 1789; ten were ratified by three-fourths of the state legislatures on 15 December 1791. The Fourth guarantees the people's right to be secure in their persons, houses, papers and effects against unreasonable searches and seizures and requires warrants based on probable cause that particularly describe what is to be searched and seized. Virginia's Declaration of Rights of 12 June 1776 had already called general warrants 'grievous and oppressive'.",
