      contribution: "Toronto-born Doctorow, a former European director of the Electronic Frontier Foundation and co-founder of the UK's Open Rights Group, writes fiction and non-fiction about surveillance, including the young-adult novel Little Brother and the book How to Destroy Surveillance Capitalism. With EFF technologist Bennett Cyphers he co-wrote the February 2021 white paper Privacy Without Monopoly, which argues that big platforms' privacy failures and their market power are linked. It proposed mandates for data portability, back-end interoperability and 'delegability' — letting users' own software act on platforms for them.",
